{
  "name": "Soul Fragments",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "RvdtHH6BB1NKOO9O",
  "img": "icons/commodities/gems/gem-rough-cushion-violet.webp",
  "folder": "43lHaixCR7Jsrr5m",
  "sort": 500000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You harvest the energy of souls to fuel some of your powers. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you gain a number of soul fragments equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one); each is a Tiny crystal object. They last until you finish another Long Rest, when they disintegrate. If you ever move more than 30 feet from a fragment, it immediately teleports to you, somewhere on your person. If a soul fragment effect requires a saving throw, the DC equals your Ranger spell save DC.</p><p>The number of fragments you gain when you finish a Long Rest increases at Ranger levels 13 (Wisdom modifier plus one) and 17 (Wisdom modifier plus two).</p><p><strong>Using Soul Fragments.</strong> You can use soul fragments in the following ways.</p><p><strong>Double Jump.</strong> You can expend one soul fragment to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplFeatherFal]{Feather Fall} or @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplJump000000]{Jump} without expending a spell slot.</p><p><strong>Soul Cleave.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you take the Attack action, you can expend one soul fragment and replace one of your attacks with a whirlwind of soul energy. Each creature in a 10-foot Emanation originating from you makes a Dexterity saving throw; on a failure, it takes Psychic damage equal to 1d12 plus your Wisdom modifier, and you regain Hit Points equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p><p><strong>Regaining Soul Fragments.</strong> When an enemy you can see within 30 feet of you dies, you can take a Reaction to regain one expended soul fragment.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-9vwYbB7HKP9xSDBK\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The uses are your soul fragments. Soul Cleave heals you only if at least one creature fails its save.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
